Chromium 157.0.8103.30 -> 157.0.8103.34, for the 157.0.8103.30 tarball.

157.0.8103.34 is a tag on the 157 branch (refs/branch-heads/8103) that has
no source tarball (as of 2026-10-31). It has the fixes made after
157.0.8103.30 up to it: those of 157.0.8103.32 and .33 (use-after-frees in
the bookmarks side panel, MojoCdm, chrome.windows.update and
TransitionPseudoElementData; HttpCache range responses; File System Access's
sensitive paths; ...), and since .33: media controls made read-only; the
display lock and Length/CalculationValue tracing fixes; ~/.cache in the File
System Access blocklist; encoding detection's TLD hint; paste sanitization of
SVG <use>; WebRTC's EmptyNetworkManager; the image cache not following
symlinks; Background Fetch keeping CORS on retry; CopySharedImage rejecting
empty rects; WebXR opaque framebuffers on session end; V8's
JSGetTemplateObject, maps, prototypes and Maglev; Skia's SkRgnBuilder heap
out-of-bounds write, SkSL raster pipeline branches and Graphite's clip
inflation and paint keys; a DevTools lit fix.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags (chromium/src
refs/tags/157.0.8103.30..157.0.8103.34), DevTools, Skia and V8 (the only
dependencies whose DEPS revisions changed; no CIPD/GCS package or gclient
gn arg changed), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations, CI configuration, PGO pointers, submodule pointer updates,
DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h and
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h; commit
67b1826c23115ecbaaaa47d96ff5e3e18f966ba1, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1005}).
Dawn's stamps and build/util/MINIBRANCH don't change.

Checked: applies to the 157.0.8103.30 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
157.0.8103.34; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag; the 157.0.8103.30 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

